<newsitem itemid="187235" id="root" date="1996-11-13" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Willis nine mths pretax profit rises 17 pct.</title>
<headline>Willis nine mths pretax profit rises 17 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 13.2		   vs 11.2</p>
<p> Quarterly div (pence)   1.65		   vs 1.65</p>
<p> Pretax			88.2		   vs 75.3</p>
<p> Turnover		    568.5		  vs 544.3</p>
<p> Brokerage and fees	534.5		  vs 510.3</p>
<p> Investment income	 34.0		   vs 34.0</p>
<p> Operating result	  84.8		   vs 69.6</p>
<p> Interest		    1.9		    vs 5.6</p>
<p> Tax			   32.7		   vs 27.8</p>
<p> Net taxed		   55.5		   vs 47.5</p>
<p> Retained earnings	 34.7		   vs 26.4</p>
<p> Pay date		    January 2 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date   December 3 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on nine month pre-tax profits for insurance broker Willis Corroon Plc were in a range of 73.0 to 80.5 million stg.</p>
<p>The result includes 8.2 million stg net profit commission receivable by the group's Lloyd's members' agency following implementation of the Lloyd's reconstruction and renewal plan, after contributions totalling 6.3 million stg to the settlement in respect of the group's broking and agency operations.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
